[test-suite name=code-diagram
  [doc [#
# CX code_diagram + code_tree Conformance Suite
Version: 0.1 — 2026-05-23 (gate 37.10 scaffold).

This file is the conformance home for `cx_code_diagram` (Mermaid
text — `flowchart TD` for code sources, `erDiagram` for data
sources) and `cx_code_tree` (JSON).

Comparison against `:expected` is **structural**
node-set + edge-set for Mermaid; key-order- and whitespace-tolerant
recursive tree-shape compare for JSON. Byte-identical output is
NOT required. See [`scripts/check_code_diagram_fixtures.py`](../scripts/check_code_diagram_fixtures.py)
for the canonical runner.

---

## Status

**Gate 37.10** (spec/v0_8_0_status.md §11.6) — this file + runner
+ `make test-code-diagram` wired. Initial scaffold (this commit):
29 fixtures across the four taxonomies (ERD / CFG / Tree / auto-
detection). The V-side emitter (`cx_code_diagram`,
`cx_code_tree`) lands in Phase 7.1 / 7.6 / 7.7; the runner skips
gracefully on missing binary so this file can stage immediately.

---

## Format

Each fixture is a block of the form:


The `view` slot selects the ABI export under test:
- `view: graph` → runner invokes `cx_code_diagram(source)` and
  compares Mermaid node-set + edge-set against `:expected`.
- `view: tree` → runner invokes `cx_code_tree(source)` and
  compares parsed JSON structurally; `loc` fields are validated for
  presence + `start < end` + substring-of-source.

`kind` is informational + cross-checks the auto-detect rule.
Absent `kind` ⇒ auto-derive (code if source has ≥ 1 top-level
EvalDirective `[?Name ...]`, else data; `[?cx ...]` PIs do NOT
count).

`level` selects the detail level:
- `min` — shape-only overview (entity boxes for ERD, def boxes for
  CFG, actor lanes only for SEQ).
- `compact` — default. Preserves the baseline detail contracts.
- `full` — exhaustive. Adds INPUT/OUTPUT terminals (CFG), synthetic
  DOCUMENT root (ERD), policy parameter notes (SEQ).

Absent `level` ⇒ `compact` (existing fixtures without a `level` line
preserve their baseline expectations).

---

## Categories

- **erd** — Graph View ERD mode (data sources).
- **cfg** — Graph View CFG mode (code sources).
- **tree** — Tree View JSON (universal).
- **auto** — Auto-detection edge cases.

---

